                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "It's a cool game. Shooter part of the original has been greatly improved, and the atmosphere of the station feels different yet similar enough. Each gun is fun to use, and ammo scarcity doesn't feel like it's forcing you to rollback to infinite ammo energy gun. However, taking too much damage might. Some controls will take time to get used, and you might want to change your keybinds as soon as you get control of your character. Also, I would recomend turning on \"play audio logs on pick up\" option. \r\n\r\nWhat I didn't like was the respawn mechanic. It felt more aggravating than just loading a save, but if you are fine with it, then you won't lose progress on death, I guess. Except for bosses because they are a forced loss. So, save at least sometimes.\r\n\r\nAlso, when I finished the game, I got an achievement for finishing the game, and defeating the big bad. The first one has a higher completion rate, but I already seen other \"bad endings\", so not sure what I missed.",
